from pathlib import Path
import json,html
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;s=json.loads((R/'SUMMARY.json').read_text())
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in [r['density'],r['lengths'],r['pool'],r['scenario'],r['flags'],r['infeasible'],round(r['medianV'],2) if r['medianV'] is not None else None,round(r['mean_expected_gap'],3) if r['mean_expected_gap'] is not None else None,round(r['mean_observed_gap'],3) if r['mean_observed_gap'] is not None else None,r['criterion_pass']])+'</tr>' for r in s)
doc='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Effect dilution and comparable bodies</title><style>body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1250px;margin:40px auto;padding:20px;background:#f8faf7;color:#173c30}td,th{padding:7px;border-bottom:1px solid #c5d4c9;text-align:left}table{border-collapse:collapse}</style><h1>Effect dilution versus matching support</h1>
<p>Frozen paired diagnosis. Four hundred fresh token layouts, each evaluated with one versus twelve exact bodies and three outcome scenarios:2,400 records. Body alternatives and outcome scenarios share layout/uniform draws; they are paired comparisons, not independent datasets. No manuscript files loaded. H/F remain separate.</p>
<p>Changing body pool alters comparability without altering token positions, variants, missingness or outcomes. Changing the planted rule adjusts qok probabilities only at available nonorigin followers. Calibrated positives target10% after ch and25% after sh across all readable interior origins. The old diluted rule applies those probabilities only at available followers, shrinking the global effect. Infeasible target probabilities are retained and unscored.</p>
<table><tr><th>Origin density</th><th>Lengths</th><th>Bodies</th><th>Scenario</th><th>Flags/100</th><th>Infeasible</th><th>Median V</th><th>Expected gap</th><th>Observed gap</th><th>Gate</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>
<p>Gaps are probability differences, not relative percentages. Calibration matches the expected all-origin effect, not each realized draw or the conditional contrast within selected pairs. That distinction limits causal attribution from power changes. The calibrated construction depends on prefix-specific availability and is a positive-power diagnostic, not a null generator.</p>
<p>The null uses independent qok draws on available followers and is not calibrated using prefix-specific margins. Some finite layouts can have small expected global differences due to unequal availability; the conditional randomization remains the object under test. Every null failure, low-power result and non-estimable case remains recorded.</p>
<p>The one-body scenario is deliberately favorable, not a realistic vocabulary claim. Variable lengths,12bodies and2%unknownslots are authored stress controls, not fitted manuscript data. Fixed versus variable length also changes length distribution and token quantity, so it is not a pure isolated length-stratification intervention. The clean body-pool comparison is paired within each layout.</p>
<p>All scoring uses the unchanged all-interior exact matching/null with Bonferroni8. A positive gate requires Wilson95 lower power≥.80; null upper flag bound≤.10. The table is a diagnostic, not manuscript qualification. No rules or thresholds were adjusted after outcomes.</p>
<p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen rules</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Hashes</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.json">Complete summaries</a> · <a href="TRIALS.json">Every result</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a></p>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(doc,encoding='utf-8')
assert all((R/f).exists() for f in ['PROTOCOL.json','FREEZE.json','SUMMARY.json','TRIALS.json','VERIFICATION.json'])
for r in s:print(r['density'],r['lengths'],r['pool'],r['scenario'],r['flags'],r['infeasible'],round(r['mean_expected_gap'] or 0,3),round(r['medianV'] or 0,2))
